With this in mind, you are tasked to prove the following target statement.

Target Problem (your task):

\begin{lemma}
\label{lemma:type3-b-ii-1-relation-between-u1}
Let $v$ and $v'$ be two vertices with $\mathit{nextM}(v)\neq\bot$ and $\mathit{nextM}(v')\neq\bot$, such that $S(v')=S(v)$ and $v'$ is a proper descendant of $v$. If $U_1(v')=\emptyset$, then $U_1(v)=\emptyset$. If $U_1(v')\neq\emptyset$, then the lowest vertex in $U_1(v)$ (if it exists) is greater than, or equal to, the greatest vertex in $U_1(v')$.
\end{lemma}

